# FastAPI Conventions

## Routes
- Always use `async def` for route handlers
- Use `Jinja2Templates` from `fastapi.templating` for all HTML rendering
- Detect HTMX requests via header: `request.headers.get("HX-Request")`
- Return HTML fragments for HTMX requests, JSON for API endpoints
- Mount static files using `StaticFiles` from `fastapi.staticfiles`

## Example route pattern
```python
@router.get("/section/{section_name}")
async def section_view(request: Request, section_name: str) -> HTMLResponse:
    data = get_section_data(section_name)  # from data_utils
    if request.headers.get("HX-Request"):
        return templates.TemplateResponse(
            f"partials/{section_name}.html",
            {"request": request, "data": data}
        )
    return templates.TemplateResponse(
        "index.html",
        {"request": request, "data": data}
    )
```

## Type Hints & Validation
- Type hints are required on all functions — FastAPI depends on them
- Use Pydantic models for any request/response schemas
- Never use bare `dict` as a return type where a model can be defined

## Code Style
- Docstrings on all route handlers and utility functions
- Keep route files thin — business logic belongs in utility modules (e.g. `data_utils.py`)
- Group related routes using `APIRouter`

## Dev Server
Run with: `uvicorn main:app --reload`
